       "text": "Goodbye.",
       "next": -1
      }
     ],
     "teach": "",
     "teachSigil": false
    },
    {
     "text": "Did he. Then he still owes me a kettle. Well. You'll want the cold, I expect. Everyone does, once fire's been at them.",
     "replies": [
      {
       "text": "Teach me.",
       "next": 3
      },
      {
       "text": "What's down here?",
       "next": 2
      }
     ],
     "teach": "",
     "teachSigil": false
    },
    {
     "text": "Cellars, then the Warden's hall. The Warden was a keeper once. Now it only keeps. East, past the acid. Bring something that breaks.",
     "replies": [
      {
       "text": "Teach me the cold.",
       "next": 3
      },
      {
       "text": "Goodbye.",
       "next": -1
      }
     ],
     "teach": "",
     "teachSigil": false
    },
    {
     "text": "There. Cooling. Draw it into a spell and the spell runs cold: water stiffens to ice, fire falters. Use it kindly.",
     "replies": [
      {
       "text": "Thank you, Sister.",
       "next": -1
      }
     ],
